---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import Disclosure from '../components/Disclosure.astro';
---
<Base title="Chambers for athletes and clubs" description="Facility planning for sports clubs and private member clubs considering Oxynova soft-shell chambers: scheduling, cleaning, space and support. No performance promises.">
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Athletes and clubs</p>
      <h1>Planning a recovery space for a club</h1>
      <p class="lede">A shared chamber is a facilities decision as much as an equipment one. These are the questions we would settle first.</p>

      <h2>Scheduling and throughput</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>How many people will want sessions, and how long will each booking occupy the room, including set-up and cleaning between users?</li>
        <li>Who is responsible for supervising sessions, and what does the manufacturer say about supervision and training?</li>
        <li>Oxynova describes Series 9 as hosting up to two users. Ask whether that applies to your use and what the written limits are.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Hygiene and upkeep</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Ask for the manufacturer's written cleaning instructions for the liner, mattress and windows, and for approved cleaning products.</li>
        <li>Ask what inspection and replacement schedule applies to zippers, seams, hoses and filters under shared use.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Space and support</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Plan floor space, a power supply for the compressor, and a quiet place for it. Oxynova states a sound level under 60&nbsp;dBA.</li>
        <li>Confirm commercial warranty terms, delivery, installation, staff training and who to call if a chamber is out of service.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="notice warn"><strong>Before you offer sessions.</strong> A club that offers sessions should get written guidance on user screening and liability from the manufacturer, its insurer and a qualified clinician.</div>

      <div class="cta-row"><CTA label="Explore manufacturer options" placement="clubs" /><a class="btn ghost" href="/chambers/">Compare models</a></div>
      <p class="cta-note">Opens oxynova.com. Independent Oxynova affiliate; we may earn a commission when you purchase through our links.</p>
      <Disclosure />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
